      "claim_id": "replication-source-replica-flow",
      "text": "Replication transfers source binary log events to a replica relay log and applies them; source commit and replica application are distinct stages, so asynchronous replication has a lag/staleness boundary.",
      "source_ids": ["mysql-replication-implementation", "mysql-binlog-overview"],
      "answer_locations": ["1 分钟版", "3 分钟版", "原理机制", "常见追问"]
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "binlog-recovery-boundary",
      "text": "The binary log records changes for replication and point-in-time recovery, while InnoDB redo log serves crash recovery; binlog retention must preserve the required recovery and replica catch-up window.",
